      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "L1 explicitly states the tag is inserted between mature residues 4 and 5 of the alpha-4 subunit. With the signal peptide spanning canonical residues 1\u201335, mature residue 4 maps to canonical position 39 (K) and mature residue 5 to canonical position 40 (E), confirmed by reading the numbered sequence. Position 39 lies deep within the large extracellular N-terminal domain (36\u2013257), 219 residues from the TM1 boundary, providing ample steric room for a short epitope tag. L2/L3 (PMC3371167) corroborate that FLAG tagging of GABRA4 alpha-4 is surface-tolerated and electrophysiologically functional, but those clips name no residue and cannot ground a separate site. FLAG (DYKDDDDK) or HA (YPYDVPDYA) epitopes inserted between mature residues 4 and 5 of GABRA4 (alpha-4 subunit) in full-length, membrane-anchored constructs expressed in mammalian cells; total and cell-surface expression measured by flow cytometry. A second independent paper (PMC3371167, L2/L3) reports a 3xFLAG-tagged alpha-4 construct with confirmed surface immunoreactivity and electrophysiological GABA responses comparable to untagged alpha-4, but does not state the insertion position and therefore cannot ground an independent site.",
